## How to Use This in Your Compass Component

Here is a minimal example showing how clean your UI code becomes when consuming `useSensors`:

```tsx
// src/components/CompassView.tsx
import React from 'react';
import { useSensors } from '../hooks/useSensors';

export const CompassView: React.FC<{ target: { lat: number; lng: number; name: string } }> = ({ target }) => {
  const { needleAngle, distanceMeters, isFacingTarget, permissionGranted, requestCompassPermission } = useSensors(target);

  return (
    <div className="flex flex-col items-center justify-center min-h-screen bg-slate-950 text-white p-6">
      {!permissionGranted && (
        <button 
          onClick={requestCompassPermission}
          className="mb-8 px-5 py-2.5 bg-emerald-500 rounded-full font-semibold shadow-lg"
        >
          Enable Compass & Walking Sensors
        </button>
      )}

      {/* Walking Distance Counter */}
      <div className="text-center mb-10">
        <h2 className="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">{distanceMeters}m</h2>
        <p className="text-slate-400 text-sm mt-1">Walking to {target.name}</p>
      </div>

      {/* Compass Needle Wheel */}
      <div className={`relative w-64 h-64 rounded-full border-2 transition-colors duration-300 flex items-center justify-center ${
        isFacingTarget ? 'border-emerald-400 bg-emerald-950/20' : 'border-slate-800'
      }`}>
        {/* Needle Arrow rotates smoothly */}
        <div 
          className="w-full h-full flex items-center justify-center transition-transform duration-100 ease-out"
          style={{ transform: `rotate(${needleAngle}deg)` }}
        >
          <div className="w-4 h-24 bg-gradient-to-t from-transparent via-emerald-400 to-emerald-300 rounded-t-full shadow-[0_0_15px_rgba(52,211,153,0.6)]" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <p className="mt-8 text-xs text-slate-500 uppercase tracking-widest">
        {isFacingTarget ? '✓ On Course (Pocket Phone)' : 'Turn to align with arrow'}
      </p>
    </div>
  );
};
```

To implement **Phase 4 (Compass UI & Hands-Free Walk Experience)**, we must design the interface around a single rule: **the user should never look at the screen for more than 3 seconds at a time.**

Below is the complete architectural blueprint and code implementation for Phase 4, organized into three coordinated components, the audio/haptic feedback engine, and the main walk screen.

---

### Architecture Overview

